  "title": "Erdős Problem #700",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $ f(n)=\\min_{1<k\\leq n/2}\\textrm{gcd}\\left(n,\\binom{n}{k}\\right). $ {UL}\n{LI}Characterise those composite $n$ such that $f(n)=n/P(n)$, where $P(n)$ is the largest prime dividing $n$.{/LI}\n{LI}Are there infinitely many composite $n$ such that $f(n)>n^{1/2}$?{/LI}\n{LI} Is it true that, for every composite $n$, $ f(n) \\ll_A \\frac{n}{(\\log n)^A} $ for every $A>0$?{/LI}\n{/UL}",
    "sha256": "bece37bc339cd0e0548f7f941ce41078f5ed7efc016a3cc1d04a374b3b42db38",
